ructure (Last-In, First-Out) using a Python class and tests push, pop, peek, size, and is_empty.\",\n34:     code: `class Stack:\n35:     def __init__(self):\n36:         self.items = []\n37: \n38:     def push(self, item):\n39:         self.items.append(item)\n40: \n41:     def pop(self):\n42:         if not self.is_empty():\n43:             return self.items.pop()\n44:         return None\n45: \n46:     def peek(self):\n47:         if not self.is_empty():\n48:             return self.items[-1]\n49:         return None\n50: \n51:     def is_empty(self):\n52:         return len(self.items) == 0\n53: \n54:     def size(self):\n55:         return len(self.items)\n56: \n57: \n58: # Example usage\n59: s = Stack()\n60: s.push(10)\n61: s.push(20)\n62: s.push(30)\n63: \n64: print(s.pop())    # 30\n65: print(s.peek())   # 20\n66: print(s.size())   # 2\n67: print(s.is_empty())  # False`\n68:   },\n69:   binary_search: {\n70:     title: \"Binary Search (Two Pointers: left, right, mid)\",\n71:     defaultInput: \"arr = [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13], target = 7\",\n72:     algorithmOverview:\n73:       \"This code searches a sorted list for a target number by checking the middle index (mid) and cutting the search range (left to right) in half.\",\n74:     code: `def binary_search(arr, target):\n75:     left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n76: \n77:     while left <= right:\n78:         mid = (left + right) // 2\n79: \n80:         if arr[mid] == target:\n81:             return mid\n82:         elif arr[mid] < target:\n83:             left = mid + 1\n84:         else:\n85:             right = mid - 1\n86: \n87:     return -1`\n88:   },\n89:   recursion_factorial: {\n90:     title: \"Recursion & Call Stack Scopes (Factorial)\",\n91:     defaultInput: \"n = 4\",\n92:     algorithmOverview:\n93:       \"This code calculates the factorial of n (4 * 3 * 2 * 1 = 24) by creating isolated Local Scope frames on the call stack.\",\n94:     code: `def factorial(k: int) -> int:\n95:     if k <= 1:\n96:         return 1\n97:     sub = factorial(k - 1)\n98:     return k * sub\n99: \n100: ans = factorial(n)\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
